CS2102 MiniProject 2026 - IITPSx assembler and emulator
Name: <your name>        User id: <your id>

Build:   make            (or: gcc asm.c -o asm ; gcc emu.c -o emu)
Test:    make test       (writes testNN.lst, testNN.o and testNN.log)
Compile flags checked: gcc -std=c89 -pedantic -W -Wall -Wpointer-arith
                       -Wwrite-strings -Wstrict-prototypes   (no warnings)

==========================  GENERAL  ==========================
[x] Source files carry my name, user id and a declaration of authorship
    (asm.c, emu.c).
[x] Compile without error under -std=c89 -pedantic.
[x] Compile without warnings under the full flag set above.
[x] Consistent formatting, sectioned program structure, descriptive
    names and explanatory comments on every function and type.

==========================  ASSEMBLER (asm.c)  ==========================
[x] Single routine (run_pass) used for both passes; pass 1 emits no code
    and does not fail on undefined labels, pass 2 emits code and does.
[x] Diagnoses label errors: duplicate label, no such label, bogus label
    name. Also: unknown mnemonic, bad number, number out of range,
    missing operand, unexpected operand, extra text on a line, operand
    not fitting in 24 bits, over-long line. Errors are sorted by line
    number. (evidence: test02.log, test06.log)
[x] Warning for labels that are defined but never used (test01.log).
[x] Listing file (.lst) - simple memory dump content and ADVANCED format:
    address, 32-bit word and mnemonic/operand, plus label lines such as
    "00000005 next:". Numeric branch offsets are shown as a label when
    the target has one.
[x] Binary object file (.o): 32-bit words, least significant byte first.
[x] Table of instruction names, opcodes and operand kinds (instr_table).
[x] Assembles the sample test program (test01).
[x] Additional test programs for success and failure with explanatory
    comments in each file (test02 - test15, bubblesort.asm).
[x] SET implemented and demonstrated (test03, also test06 for SET errors).
[x] mul and div implemented and demonstrated (test04, test08, test09).
[x] Bubble sort program (bubblesort.asm): assembles and works - the
    array is sorted in place (bubblesort.log).

==========================  EMULATOR (emu.c)  ==========================
[x] Loads the object file produced by asm.
[x] Memory dump before and after execution (-before, -after); also
    -trace, -isa and -limit options.
[x] Executes the test programs (test01 - test15, bubblesort).
[x] Executes mul and div correctly, including detection of division by
    zero (test04, test08, test09, test11).
[x] Detects errant programs: PC out of range (test12), infinite loop via
    an instruction limit (test13), illegal opcode (test14), memory access
    out of range (test15), invalid shift count, division overflow.

